WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.730
- Hi everyone, my name is Heinrich,

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.260
and welcome to another coffee
break with Firm Learning.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.960
I hope you all had a good week.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.630
Today the weather is
super bad here in Germany,

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:12.150
and I was sitting alone at my desk today,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.120
and I asked myself, what
other topic Can I bring you

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.910
that will really make a
difference in your work life.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.950
And one of the things

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.140
that quickly came to my mind is feedback.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.650
How to actually give good
feedback that is received well,

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.600
and actually valuable for
the person who receives this.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.980
And my experience,

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.760
this is something that
many people struggle with.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.940
In my career, I received
many pieces of bad feedback.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.900
Bad feedback for me is a
feedback that makes me feel bad

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.820
after I leave the conversation,
and doesn't really help me

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.310
to improve my actual work.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.730
This is bad feedback because
it's no value add for everybody

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.270
is just losers leaving the table.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.760
And just to help you better
understand the difference.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.190
I'd like to contrast two managers of mine

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.650
in the past in consulting career.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.530
One manager, there was a
situation where I was creating

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.760
a PowerPoint document,
and he was reviewing it

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.240
as a pretty much happens every
single day in consulting.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.910
So he was going through the pages,

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:14.620
and then there was one important page,

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.440
and we were sitting together,
and he was saying something

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.077
like, "Yeah, I pretty like this,
probably we can change this

00:01:21.077 --> 00:01:23.547
"and let this be shown a bit differently,

00:01:23.547 --> 00:01:25.460
"and let's change the text here a bit."

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.840
And then he was basically
doing it on the piece of paper,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.739
and giving it to me, and
thank you please improve.

00:01:29.739 --> 00:01:32.810
And that was for me, okay,
in the beginning he said,

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.270
he was fine with it, I mean,

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:36.610
he pretty much changed
the whole page afterwards.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.830
But it was okay, I knew
what was happening,

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.800
and I kind of took his
points and thought myself,

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.020
how can I improve for the future, right?

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.150
This being contrasted
with another manager,

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.120
pretty much same situation,
I was working on a deck,

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.260
he was reviewing it, and
he was looking at a page,

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.277
and pretty much was saying,

00:01:54.277 --> 00:01:58.330
"Heinrich this is complete
garbage, please do that again."

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.490
What is the impact of that on me?

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:03.130
Of course, I feel bad, I
feel like I created garbage,

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.440
which of course nobody wants to create.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.800
And it also didn't really have me to know

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.520
how I can actually approve
it and make it better.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.630
And I hope just taking
this as a starting point,

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:15.300
it becomes clear that how
you deliver the feedback

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.970
really makes a difference.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:20.370
And it can either help
somebody, built him up

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.540
and help him to make a
better work next time.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.350
Or it can leave somebody just hurt,

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.740
and without any clue on
how to improve the job.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.790
If you're in the early
years of your career,

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:32.550
you might ask yourself,
Well, why do I actually need

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:34.310
to know how to give feedback anyways,

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.570
isn't just the others
who will give feedback

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.860
to me in the beginning?

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.450
And why this for sure might be true.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.446
Usually, there are several instances

00:02:42.446 --> 00:02:43.480
where you can use this, right?

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:46.930
Often pretty early on you at
some point get maybe an intern

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.260
you work with, and then you would like

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:49.940
to give feedback to the intern.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.340
Or also many organizations if you actually

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.630
do a feedback session
with one of your managers,

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.640
of course in the beginning,
you get the feedback

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.140
from the manager, but
then usually there's also

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.714
an opportunity where you can get feedback

00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:04.050
to the manager, right?

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.530
Because the manager
wants to improve as well.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.420
Yes, this does depend on the culture

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.250
of this actually something that happens.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.320
But in many organizations,
this is how it's done.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.660
And before I'd like to
give you a framework

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.020
on how you can actually
structure and deliver

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.147
your feedback in a constructive way,

00:03:20.147 --> 00:03:22.710
let me make two preliminary remarks,

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.300
which I believe are really crucial

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.560
to the whole feedback thing, right?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.110
And the first thing is that
you need to distinguish

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.810
the person from an action or a task.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.030
I believe that it is almost
never had fully constructive

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.480
to say, you are a bad
person, you can't do it,

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.710
you are not ready for the job, right?

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:48.120
Because things like that, I
wouldn't even consider feedback.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.670
This is pretty much just
an insight that is about

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:53.530
to just bring that person down,

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:56.250
and it's not helping the person at all.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.950
If you would like to get feedback,

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.880
never directly related to the person,

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.010
but make it about the work,
on action of the person.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:09.090
Don't say you did a crappy
job, but rather say,

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:12.090
the document that you created,
the work that you did,

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:16.900
just didn't met the expectations,
or the thing that you did

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.350
in that specific meeting or
on that specific instance,

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.890
from my perspective isn't the right

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.310
for these reasons, right?

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:27.060
So always talk about actions or the work,

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.800
but never talk about an
attribute of the person himself,

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.650
don't criticize the character of a person,

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.060
because this is not giving feedback,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.690
this is just being offensive.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.960
The second general remark is
that you should always be aware

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.130
that what you're saying
is your perception,

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:47.150
your personal perception,
and for two reasons.

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:49.850
First, for yourself
also you need to realize

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.200
that your perception is subjective, right?

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.650
So it's your opinion due to
all the things that you have

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.600
in your head and the way you
were educated and raised,

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:03.300
that you a specific thing to
do is wrong or doesn't work,

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.030
but maybe another person

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.680
has a different
perspective on that, right?

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.187
And for this reason, it's
important to use I messages.

00:05:12.187 --> 00:05:17.187
So to use things like, I
believe this is wrong, right?

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:20.680
Or in my perception, the
work that you delivered

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.520
is not meeting the standard.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:27.270
Don't just say it as a
general rule of nature,

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.490
that the specific things
that another person does

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.430
are wrong or are not working
or whatever, but rather,

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.920
make it clear that this is
your specific perception.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.040
And the one side of this is
that, this is humility, right?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.020
You acknowledge that maybe other people

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.000
might have other perceptions.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.000
And maybe also, in some instances,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.830
you believe this is rather likely,

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:48.663
I mean, it's possible, right?

00:05:48.663 --> 00:05:51.600
But the other side of that is that,

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:55.220
your perception is never wrong, right?

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:59.430
In the sense that another
person cannot tell you that,

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:01.430
no, you didn't have the perception, right?

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:04.770
So if you bring a point of
feedback to the other person,

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:09.470
if you phrase it as an I
message, and the person says,

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.060
I don't believe that,
I don't agree with you.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:13.500
You can always say, well, you know,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.780
I'm talking about my
perceptions, believe it or not,

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:18.670
but this is the perception
that I have, right?

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.970
And it's pretty much
impossible for the other person

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:23.770
to say that you cannot
have the processional,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.830
you are not allowed to
have the perception,

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.650
this is not actually your perception,

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.367
because well, it is the perception, right?

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.890
And now we can argue whether
it's justified or not,

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.010
but this is the perception that I have

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.730
when looking at your work, right?

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.180
So you may be I have another opinion,

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.370
but still my perception is that

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:42.400
this piece of work is subpar, right?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.370
So this is of course, an
important way how to phrase it.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:49.230
So now to framework that you
can use to give your feedback.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.690
This framework has four
steps, and from my experience

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:56.250
if you use this framework
to deliver your feedback,

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.660
very rarely somebody leaves
the conversation deeply hurt,

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:03.170
and almost always, there
some constructive point

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.600
that the other person can take
out of your feedback, right?

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.210
So what are the first steps?

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:11.000
The first step is, clearly
state your perception

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.270
in an I message just in the way

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.730
that we talked about it, right?

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.950
So say, I perceived
that you did this work,

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.830
and from my perspective,

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:22.200
this is just not the way
it's supposed to be, right?

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.430
So start with an I message,
with the perception

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:28.630
that you share to make a
specific point of feedback.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.690
The second point is, give examples.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:36.630
So names specific instances
where you observed

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:38.890
the things that you
would like to talk about

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:42.100
to make a tangible and to
not make a just an assertion,

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.270
but rather something based on facts.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.650
So say, for instance,
you know, when I looked

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.130
at the document that
you handed over to me,

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:53.560
I saw that you wrote this
thing in this specific way,

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.370
which in my perception isn't
good for these reasons, right?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.070
And now this is the third
point, tell the person

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:04.050
why you believe that a certain
action or a certain behavior,

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:08.190
or piece of work that the person
competed is maybe not good,

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.280
and tell them why this
is actually relevant,

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.570
why is it important
that the person does it

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:16.150
in a specific thing, explain
to him so that it's intuitive

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.380
and insightful for the person

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.280
why he actually needs to change.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.820
And then the fourth thing
important, give an advice,

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:26.850
give a recommendation, how the
person actually can improve

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.940
and change the way, maybe
from your experience

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:32.180
what you learned when you
were younger, whatever,

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.690
try to help the person how
to actually improve the work.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.610
Don't just tell them that
what is doing is wrong,

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.720
it doesn't work, et cetera,

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.840
but try to give him something

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.090
that he can work with in order to improve.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.154
So now let's make an example

00:08:44.154 --> 00:08:46.150
of how that could work out, right?

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:49.310
Let's pretend that we are
having a feedback conversation.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.740
And you are junior colleague of mine.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.530
And actually, I'm noticing
that in many of your pieces

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.020
of work, you make lots of
orthographical and grammar errors,

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.460
and I'd like to give you
that feedback, right?

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:04.030
So we could sit together
and I could open something

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:06.760
like, hey, I'd like to give
you just a point of feedback

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:08.270
if that's okay for you.

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.350
I was reviewing your work
recently and on several instances

00:09:11.350 --> 00:09:14.540
in my perspective, I'm
noticing that you are doing

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:17.020
quite a lot of orthographical
and grammar errors,

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:19.650
and actually much more
from what I would expect

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.730
is appropriate and would
be expected in your role.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.720
Let me give you a few examples

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.530
so that you know what I'm talking about.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:29.150
So the board document
that we created yesterday,

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.470
I was reading it, and
before we were actually able

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.460
to send it out, I fixed over
10 orthographical errors.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.510
In another instance last week,
you wrote the press release,

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.670
if you may remember it, and in there,

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:43.597
there were these four errors that I fixed.

00:09:43.597 --> 00:09:46.900
So these are now, these two
instances where you made

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:49.940
quite a couple of lots of
orthographical and grammar errors

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:53.510
in your piece of work, and
this isn't great, right?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.256
And also for you to help you understand,

00:09:55.256 --> 00:09:58.070
just doesn't work because
we work in consulting

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.110
with clients, our clients
pay, of course, a lot of money

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:02.760
as we all know for services,

00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:05.530
and they expect highest levels of quality

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:06.980
in the work that we deliver.

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:09.300
And if they see a piece of paper from us,

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.730
which contains this amount of errors,

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.350
actually any error at all,

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:16.960
it might cast the shadow on our work,

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:19.080
that we're actually not
giving attention to details,

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.650
that we don't really care,
that we are not really giving

00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:25.520
our best to make that piece of
work the best that we can do,

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.360
and this is just not meeting
the professional standards

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.450
that we have here in our organization.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:34.860
And just a few advice, a few
tips that may have helped me

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.510
in the past in order to improve,

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:39.380
so usually if I correct
an important document,

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.690
I like to print out and
then have it in front of me,

00:10:41.690 --> 00:10:43.830
and then read it, because this way,

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.680
it takes me to spot all the errors.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.950
And the second thing
that also always do is,

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:52.420
I use the the standard
orthographical error checking,

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.790
that programs like Microsoft Word have.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:57.090
So also advise you that
whenever you send out

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.830
such a document, always load
it a text editor like that,

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:01.650
and make sure that all the errors

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:03.740
that are popping up in there,

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:06.050
that you fix them before
you actually send it out.

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:08.950
So cut here, I hope you
understood where I'm heading.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:11.930
I hope you also see and
understand that, usually,

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.260
if you deliver the feedback in this way,

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:18.210
very rarely the other person
has any grounds of saying,

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.900
you know, this is unfair,
or this is not right,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.730
or this is just not the way it is, right?

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.150
Because I mean, you gave specific examples

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.170
where you base your feedback on you,

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.610
you phrase it as an I message,

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.770
you talk about your perceptions,

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.700
and its effect that you're
having these perceptions, right?

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:36.960
So the other person cannot
say you're not having them

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.430
because that is just how
it is, you have them.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:41.150
And you also try to
help the person, right?

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:44.770
So usually these leaves
everybody on a constructive note.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:49.230
And I believe that if you
deliver this feedback this way,

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.900
you would much more professionally

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.560
than many other people
do, and all your people

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.140
you work with, we just
appreciate this a lot.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.670
So let me know what you think.

00:11:57.670 --> 00:12:00.330
Do you have any
experiences on the feedback

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.750
that you received or maybe that you gave?

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.180
What are your learnings?

